      "stdout": "Upscale target segment resolution.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h,     --help              Print this help message and exit\r\n          --ref TEXT          Unified draft reference\r\n          --seg-id TEXT       Target segment id (required; raw id, no seg_id= prefix)\r\n          --mode TEXT         Target resolution tier: 1080p / 2k / 4k\r\n          --from TEXT         Source track hint, e.g. multi_track (default)\r\n          --input-path TEXT   Optional input media path override\r\n          --output-path TEXT  Optional output product path\r\n          --history-node-id TEXT \r\n                              Existing upscale history node id\r\n          --task-id TEXT      Existing upscale task id\r\n          --is-complete TEXT  Mark an existing product complete: true / false\r\n          --skip-re-run TEXT  Reuse an existing product without rerunning: true / false\r\n          --wait TEXT         Wait for the algorithm to finish: true / false (default true)\r\n          --timeout <duration> \r\n                              Execution timeout; explicit unit required, e.g. 5min or 300s\r\n  -v,     --version           Show version information and exit.\r\n          --jq TEXT           Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                              .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                              the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nEXAMPLES\r\n  # Upscale to the 4K resolution tier for one segment\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo upscale-resolution --mode 4k --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Upscale to 2K without blocking, with a custom timeout\r\n  $ lyra-cli draft algo upscale-resolution --mode 2k --wait false --timeout 5min --seg-id <UUID>\r\n  # Reuse an existing upscale product\r\n  $ lyra-cli dra